# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets --
#
# Each service also has its own .gitignore covering these. Repeated here so the
# rule holds even if one of those is edited or moved: a secret reaching a
# pushed commit cannot be taken back by deleting it later, only by rewriting
# history AND rotating the credential.
#
# backend/.env   MongoDB Atlas URI, JWT_SECRET_KEY, ADMIN_EMAILS
# compiler/.env  the same JWT secret, GEMINI_API_KEY, the Atlas URI
.env
.env.*
!.env.sample

# ------------------------------------------------------------- dependencies --
node_modules/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ builds --
dist/
build/

# --------------------------------------------------------------- test data --
#
# 4.6 GB between them, and they are the same bytes twice: the importer
# hard-links each test file rather than copying it, so these two trees share
# one copy on disk. GitHub will not take either.
#
# Neither needs to be in the repo to rebuild the judge:
#   compiler/testdata/  is regenerated by  node scripts/cses/import.cjs
#                       (CSES) and  node scripts/import/runner.js  (the rest)
#   cses_problems/      is the source archive those read from — keep it backed
#                       up somewhere that is not a git repo
cses_problems/
compiler/testdata/

# Scratch directories the judge writes submitted code into, then deletes.
compiler/codes/
compiler/outputs/

# --------------------------------------------------------------- notes, OS --
#
# Source material for the Core CS section rather than code: third-party PDFs
# and cheat sheets, some of them signed by their authors. Kept out of the repo
# because they are not ours to redistribute.
csnotes/

.DS_Store
*.log
*.bak
